Z||000000||fiero56||04-10-2001||11:02 PM||||Been all over the news lately. I haven't been paying particular attention to this story, so my details might be fuzzy:<BR>A cop shot and killed a black man, and there are now riots in the city, possibly over race? I don't know. Was just on the news that an elderly couple driving downtown was pulled out of their car by a few rioters, and were injured and taken to the hospital.<BR>I don't know the layout of Cincy, but people are urged to stay out of the west side. <P>Was also just watching 20/20 or similar talking about "open season" on anyone who attempts or succeeds in breaking into a home in S.C. Almost no matter what the circumstances, if you shoot someone in your house, attempting to get in or running away from either of the above mentioned, you are allowed to shoot them down even in the back as they run away, without any possibility of being prosecuted, jailed, or charged with any crime. My view is more power to them. This is an awsome law, that more states should adopt. The best part is it was passed due to a string of gang related home invasions. About time somebody realized how to properly fight crime. They had someone on there talking about hearing someone open his bedroom window in the middle of the night. He says the guy fell out of the window when he heard a shell being chambered. Must have scared the $hit out of him    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. When I was going to school in columbus, we had similar forms of defense, but we had baseball bats and pipe-wrenches in our kitchen. Almost got to use them a number of times too.<P>Edited for spelling errors, but couldn't get spell check to work anyway.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||1
