Z||000012||BENGAL4||04-11-2001||10:23 PM||||What a black eye for my beloved city. This whole thing has been nothing but BS. The kid that was shot, had 14 warrants for his arrest. Granted, they were traffic offenses, but when the police says stop, you stop. If this guy would have stopped, he would have been alive right now.<P>As for the protesters, most of them were just looking for trouble. They were attacking innocent people and each one of the victims are white. I am not a prejudiced person, but I can't stomach this racial hatred. Why can't we all just get along?<P>It all comes down to this, it is a total lack of respect for law and order. The big buzz phrase in Cincy lately has been "Racial Profiling" by the police. Well when 15% of the population is causing 85% of the crime, what do people expect. I used to get profiled by local cops in my muscle car days. They would see someone with long hair and they would harass us. The cops used to measure the bumper height on the back of my 69 Mach1, I allways passed, but they would stop me anyway. I guess to see if I had contraband in the car. Which they never found. It never hurt me. Well that's my .02 from a Cincinnatian.<P>Bill  ||||reg||8
Z||000013||Eric||04-11-2001||11:30 PM||||Most of us know what it's like to be profiled.  Our cars give the police something to do more often than not.  I get my tags run about once a week.  You kind of get a sick feeling in your stomach like you know you haven't done anything wrong, but you still feel guilty somehow.  So what do we do?  We just go with the flow.  We don't do anything to make the situation worse like running, and more often than not, nothing else happens.  That's probably what 99.99% of the victims of racial profiling do.  I just can't feel sympathy for someone who knew the sitiuation was going to come to a head with one dumbass move after another.  When a cop has a gun pointed at you, you stop.  You don't hike up your pants or go for you pager, because you know ,by instinct, you've been caught.  The black community in Cincy should feel relieved to rid themselves of such a anchor of stupidity.  <P>Isn't it funny how Bengal had to clarify that he's "not a racist" before he said he can't stomach racial hatred?  Anymore it's PC to be racist towards whites, just look at how the media interprets the cause of these riots.  Dragging white people out of cars just because they're white is not a reasonable and acceptable outlet for a black man's frustration.  We have to apply the same rules to EVERYBODY if we are ever going to live in a society that doesn't define itself in terms of color.||||reg||1
Z||000014||87GT||04-12-2001||09:43 PM||||I heard some more on the news today about Cincinnati still having riots.  Its getting  ridiculous now.  I noticed the media here in Tampa keeps mentioning that this young kid was the 4th or 5th black killed by Cincy police in the last 4 to 5 mths.  What I was wondering is, Have the police in Cincy been forced to kill someone of a different race in the last 4 or 5 mths?  If so, why wouldnt that be mentioned?  Just a thought.  I hope the situation there improves.  There was a riot in St. Pete a few years back because a white police officer killed a black man for trying to run over him/her in a car.  Clear self defense, but it turned into more of the same.||||reg||1
Z||000015||fiero56||04-12-2001||10:32 PM||||They are under a city-wide curfew right now. I think its 8pm-6am. With NO exception except for to/from work. <P>I had the tv on last night when an officer was shot. They interrupted programming, and mentioned the cops were saying something along the lines of: "forget the bean bags, just get your shot-guns". Must be getting pretty intense. There were a few "demonstrators" at one of the televised press conferences earlier today. They were busy shouting, interrupting the speeches, and carrying on. I guess that's one way to get your cause heard    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">. I don't think they're going to get much respect that way though.<P>87GT: according to bill, more than 4 out of 5 times, it is (I'm assuming Bill means African American)African Americans commiting crime. With that ratio(and assumming the crimes committed by other races are the same degree), if you take the 14 black deaths over the last 3 years that the news is reporting, that would mean there would be approximately 3 non African American deaths by cop in the last 3 years. I don't have hard numbers here, so this isn't written in stone, and I did the math in my head since I have no calcualtor nearby, so my numbers were rounded and estimated.<P>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-16-2001).]||||reg||1
