Z||000019||Oreif||04-13-2001||12:56 AM||||I know we have a few law enforcement folks on here, so correct me if I'm wrong. But Isn't the officer trained to protect himself and the public? According to CNN, the officer chased the suspect into an alley and the suspect made a move that the officer assumed he was going for a gun. Now with the amount of illegal guns out today and the amount of kids (of ALL races) that have them, the officer had what, maybe a 10th of a second to decide if he should shoot or not. In the officers' place I probably would have done the same. At that point the officer had to choose between himself and the suspect. I don't think the race of the kid had anything to do with it. We cannot control illegal guns, and with the amount that the average city recovers, there are many still out there. Per the news the kid did not have one. But with a 10th of a second to decide, what would you choose?<P>As for the riots, well lets just say it is wrong to riot. I'll leave it at that.||||reg||1
