Z||000038||Oreif||04-13-2001||11:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>youall ever hear about detroit in 1944 riot??<BR>tank and machineguns used on unarmed crowd resulting in hundreds of bodys that where bulldozed in to river. wartime coverup= no news coverage. my dad saw it go down.<BR>all cops are armed and dangerous some more than others so don't twitch or you may die.<BR>why can't cops be accoutable for killing and or event they caused [like this riot].</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The Detroit Riot did not have "hundreds of bodies bulldozed" There was a total of 34 people killed and 58 people injured. The Riots started on Belle Island amusement park.<BR>If your Dad was there he has an active imagination. The riot was not started by police. It was started over a group of white teenagers and  black teenagers fighting. What started with a group of 20 teenagers had escallated into some 5000 people rioting thru the night. By morning the rioting had subsided. Detroit was going thru some racial tension because many southern blacks went to detroit for work. The war effort at GM and Ford was going very strong then. Please don't corrupt the topic at hand with twisted opinions and lies. You need to study history and the real facts.<BR>Maybe you should talk to a real police officer in a major city who patrols the more violent areas. Then you might understand things from his point of view. Then again he may recognize you from your mug shot.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
