Z||000042||Black88GT||04-14-2001||05:08 PM||||First of all, my town won the Super Bowl, and there were no riots.  While its true that drunk white people sometimes riot after sporting events, its usually a one night deal where a couple cars are turned and a couple bonfires are started, after that its over.  There's no need for Curfews or Nat'l Guard protection.<P>Secondly, its easy for some of us to talk about how an unarmed man was shot.  However when your in a life or death situation with a split second to make a decision, there's no reason to question what the cop did.  Cop says stop, kid doesnt stop, chase happens then kid reaches for his pockets, well I'm gonna fire before he has the chance, plain and simple.  Would I feel bad about it later?  Most likely.  Not because I made the wrong decision but because a person lost their life because of a stupid move on there part.<P>Finally, I don't believe reverse discrimination is the answer to years of discrimination against minorities.  <P>||||reg||1
