Z||000045||Cooter||04-14-2001||08:32 PM||||My brother is a policeman and was involved in a shooting where the suspect died. Do you think it was an easy decision to make? They begged and pleaded with the man to drop his weapon. It was only when an attempt was made on another officer did my brother fire. It was hard on all of us. By not making the choice to drop his weapon, he left the officers no choice. Before you stand here and condemn these men for standing up for law and order, you should consider what it would be like if they were not on the job.||||reg||1
Z||000046||BENGAL4||04-14-2001||09:21 PM||||The law is the law. Without law, there is anarchy. I know that this crisis has angered and upset me. Cincinnati is a wonderful place to grow up and raise a family. The lawless protesters are giving my city an undeserved black eye. Granted I am not from the inner city, but I have freinds,(black and white), who were born and raised there and I know it is a different world than the one I live in. They do not live there any more because of the following question I asked some of them. <P>I asked them, What would you tell the inner city people to solve their problems? They told me this.<P>1. Fathers, take responsibility for your children and don't leave them for the mothers and the goverment to raise and support.<P>2. If you are stuck in the inner city and want to get out, EDUCATE YOURSELF. As they say educate your mind and your a$$ will follow.<P>So simple it is stupid.<P>Peace,<P>Bill<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000047||Kelvin Vivian||04-15-2001||01:09 AM||||I believe that what we have in America is a class struggle that's clothed as a race struggle. We think welfare - black, crime - black, drugs - black but tis NOT the case.<P>The majority of the people on welfare are white, the majority of the poor in America are white, the majority of the crimes committed in society are committed by those who are white, and the percentages of whites who use drugs are the same if not more than those who are black. Yet, if we look at the criminal justice system, we see that it is blacks who make up the largest percentage of those targeted. Is that fair? NO. We do not yet live in a color-blind society, with a Constitution that tolerates no classes among its citizens. Will we ever be a color-blind society? Maybe. When I was young, I was color-blind, as I grow older, I grow less so.<P>I do not think Oswald killed Kennedy. And I did not like the way the Supreme Court "decided" the outcome of the last presidential race instead of letting the political process continue to its own end. Results now show Bush would have won anyways, so be it, I don't like Courts subverting the voting process, and making lucky guesses.<P>But let one thing stand clear... I love Fieros! This is America and we can all have our opinions, I know I have mine!||||reg||1
Z||000048||Oreif||04-15-2001||02:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>you quote the gov. line on detroit riot<BR>not what realy happen as over 10 times the numbers of killed as cover up reports.<BR>dad saw the bodys being dumped, trucks loads of them ,the unreported killed not the offical count.<BR>or maybe you think the GOV never lie to us<BR>or that lee harvy oswald acted alone??<BR>if so do you want to buy a bridge????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Sorry, But the quote I list was not from any government agency. It was from a book written by the owner of the amusement park where the riot started. It has eyewitness accounts of the riot. (from both sides, and your dad wasn't in the book) It discusses the racial tension of that time. Maybe you should go to a library and check it out. It was published in 1955. Or do you think the Government paid him off. What does Lee Harvey Oswald have to do with the Detriot Riot? He was a scape goat for those that killed Kennedy. <P>As for "my people built this place", Why do you complain about what is going on? You are then stating that all the problems of today are because of you! If you would have "built" it right than we shouldn't have the problems we have today. So the next time there is a riot or school shooting we can all blame you! (Just using your narrow-minded twisted logic) <P>As for a police officer holding a gun to my head, I have never given them a reason too.<BR>Maybe you should respect them as most people do. It's the idiots that think they are smarter by hassling the officer that get into trouble. ||||reg||1
